      "name": "Türker TUNALI (ERPNext Türkiye)",
      "created_at": "2023-11-07T09:45:51.940Z",
      "cooked": "<p>We were easily set a template item price in the past. So all the variants of the template can use the same pricing strategy. Because transactions search a price for the given item first. If it can’t find, it is searching for the template price.</p>\n<p>So users apply a pricing without entering 100s of variant prices.</p>\n<p>But <a href=\"https://github.com/frappe/erpnext/pull/34189\" rel=\"noopener nofollow ugc\">this modification</a> removes the template item pricing and we don’t have a simple way to manage the variant prices.</p>\n<p>I believe that managing prices should be easy and it should work. How can we regain this feature?</p>",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/discuss.frappe.io/turkertunali/{size}/55246_2.png",
